      en: "The ruins of Sbeitla (Latin: Sufetula) are located in central Tunisia and are among the best-preserved Roman sites in North Africa. The city was founded in the 1st century AD and flourished in the 2nd and 3rd centuries. It is especially known for its Capitolium, featuring three well-preserved temples dedicated to Jupiter, Juno, and Minerva. The city included a forum, baths, a theatre, and a basilica. Sbeitla was also an early Christian centre, with several churches from the 4th and 5th centuries surviving. The site was designated a national monument in 1977 and attracts researchers and tourists interested in Roman urbanism.",
